{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/infernal-exalted/1327706-how-often-should-second-edition-infernals-gain-limit-from-violating-their-urge","id":1327706,"title":"How often should (second edition) infernals gain limit from violating their urge?","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Exalted","Infernal Exalted"],"posts":[{"date":"2019-07-27T02:13:56-07:00","id":1327706,"title":"How often should (second edition) infernals gain limit from violating their urge?","content":"If we use the usual &quot;once per scene&quot; rule it becomes problematic, because it takes away all free will. On the other side if we make it much longer then it becomes meaningless<br /> Is there any official rule about this?<br /> <br /> Also, i assume that the infernal is not obligated to fulfill the Urge in the Yozis's usual way right? That is, if i have a Malfean Urge to &quot;Kill Lytek&quot; i can do the deed in ways more reminiscent of the ebon dragon without violating the Urge, right?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1492-mark","name":"mark","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1492_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1379"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-07-27T03:23:33-07:00","id":1327711,"title":"","content":"\u201cViolating your Urge\u201d isn\u2019t the same as \u201cnot doing it this instant.\u201d If your Urge is just \u201ckill Lytek,\u201d then something like tipping him off would be a violation of your Urge, but saving a basket of puppies from a house fire would not be.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>He/him","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/177-thecountalucard","name":"TheCountAlucard","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar177_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10857"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-07-27T03:47:31-07:00","id":1327717,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>mark</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/infernal-exalted/1327706-how-often-should-second-edition-infernals-gain-limit-from-violating-their-urge#post1327706\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">If we use the usual &quot;once per scene&quot; rule it becomes problematic, because it takes away all free will. On the other side if we make it much longer then it becomes meaningless<br /> Is there any official rule about this?</div> </div> </div> </div>Abyssals have the same when they commit sins of life, having to role their essence to gain resonance. Also acts of villainy can reduce their limit.<br /> <br /> As far as limit breaking, it is only for a scene. And the urge itself is a secondary motivation, where if you act on it you get willpower back and other bonuses. It is only when you act against the urge that you roll for limit.<br /> <br /> It's something that the player and ST should define out in character creation so it does not feel like free will is being robbed.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Also, i assume that the infernal is not obligated to fulfill the Urge in the Yozis's usual way right? That is, if i have a Malfean Urge to &quot;Kill Lytek&quot; i can do the deed in ways more reminiscent of the ebon dragon without violating the Urge, right? </div> </div> </div>If you are doing ways to tear down Lytek, to weaken him for the kill, then it should not matter how you go about it. Again, per the rules you only gain limit if you act against or contrary to the urge. So if you help Lytek, you gain limit for going against the urge. If you decide to take over a city in the meantime, then limit is not rolled since you are not acting contrary to the urge.<br /> <br /> That's how I read it of course.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3012-uknown-darklord","name":"Uknown DarkLord","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3012_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"485"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-07-27T09:56:17-07:00","id":1327751,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>TheCountAlucard</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/infernal-exalted/1327706-how-often-should-second-edition-infernals-gain-limit-from-violating-their-urge?p=1327711#post1327711\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">\u201cViolating your Urge\u201d isn\u2019t the same as \u201cnot doing it this instant.\u201d If your Urge is just \u201ckill Lytek,\u201d then something like tipping him off would be a violation of your Urge, but saving a basket of puppies from a house fire would not be.</div> </div> </div> </div>But what if i just sit around in my hellish town house, doing nothing but sex with neomahs? After how much time is this considered as acting contrary to an urge","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1492-mark","name":"mark","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1492_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1379"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-07-27T10:01:51-07:00","id":1327753,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>mark</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/infernal-exalted/1327706-how-often-should-second-edition-infernals-gain-limit-from-violating-their-urge?p=1327751#post1327751\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">But what if i just sit around in my hellish town house, doing nothing but sex with neomahs?</div> </div> </div> </div>If an Abyssal does nothing but grind out knuckle-children over the Mouth of Oblivion, without ever having a Deathlord show up and tell him to cut that out, does he gain Resonance?<br /> <br /> \u200bWhy should your situation be different from his?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>He/him","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/177-thecountalucard","name":"TheCountAlucard","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar177_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10857"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-07-27T10:16:10-07:00","id":1327756,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>TheCountAlucard</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/infernal-exalted/1327706-how-often-should-second-edition-infernals-gain-limit-from-violating-their-urge?p=1327753#post1327753\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">If an Abyssal does nothing but grind out knuckle-children over the Mouth of Oblivion, without ever having a Deathlord show up and tell him to cut that out, does he gain Resonance?<br /> <br /> \u200bWhy should your situation be different from his?</div> </div> </div> </div>Because the abyssal gains resonance by committing sins of life and sins of death, not by ignoring an artificial motivation.<br /> <br /> In fact, technically speaking, said abyssal is furthering the cause of oblivion, if only in the most inefficient way possible. But having sex with Neomahs does not bring you even an inch closer to killing Lytek. Or corrupting Lytek, or subverting him, or ruining his work, etc depending on your type of Urge","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1492-mark","name":"mark","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1492_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1379"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-07-27T10:17:48-07:00","id":1327757,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>mark</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/infernal-exalted/1327706-how-often-should-second-edition-infernals-gain-limit-from-violating-their-urge#post1327706\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">If we use the usual &quot;once per scene&quot; rule it becomes problematic, because it takes away all free will. </div> </div> </div> </div>No it doesn't; harmful consequences does not mean that you're incapable of making a choice.<br /> <br /> (Free will does not exist and people almost never really make choices for entirely different reasons)<br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>mark</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/infernal-exalted/1327706-how-often-should-second-edition-infernals-gain-limit-from-violating-their-urge?p=1327751#post1327751\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">But what if i just sit around in my hellish town house, doing nothing but sex with neomahs? After how much time is this considered as acting contrary to an urge</div> </div> </div> </div>I would presume that a character acting in a manner suggesting that they're never going to try and fulfill the Urge qualifies for gaining limit.<br /> <br /> I also think your chosen example is not really a thing that would happen, least of all in an actually played game where tracking limit and Torment actually matters.<br /> <br /> That being said, the Urges of Green Sun Princess should maybe not often be something so narrow as killing a specific person, and they're stated to be something that's supposed to generally complement the motives and nature of the character.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-07-27T10:26:09-07:00","id":1327761,"title":"","content":"If you really want to give out limit for Infernals ignoring their urge you can have people remind them of it, and when they refuse to act then give out some limit, or provide obvious means of advancing their urge and when they ignore it give them some limit.<br /> <br /> Really the question of how often you want give any exalt limit depends on the kind of story that you're telling. If you want to have one of your themes be that Infernals are doomed to be monsters and a player is avoiding their urge to be less monstrous you can give out limit and limit break to force the Infernal to be more monsterous.<br /> <br /> Heck, you can do lots of story manipulation with limit breaks if you wanted. Emphasis the limit break can be cathartic or even addictive by forcing a situation when a character is low on Willpower and desperately needs more at the same time the character needs just one more limit to limit break then offer the opportunity for that last point of limit. Now, you have a character that just got a ton of value out of limit break and a player that may actively seem out limit break.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/151-hark","name":"Hark","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar151_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"932"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-07-27T10:31:36-07:00","id":1327762,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Isator Levi</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/infernal-exalted/1327706-how-often-should-second-edition-infernals-gain-limit-from-violating-their-urge?p=1327757#post1327757\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> No it doesn't; harmful consequences does not mean that you're incapable of making a choice.<br /> <br /> (Free will does not exist and people almost never really make choices for entirely different reasons)<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> I would presume that a character acting in a manner suggesting that they're never going to try and fulfill the Urge qualifies for gaining limit.<br /> <br /> I also think your chosen example is not really a thing that would happen, least of all in an actually played game where tracking limit and Torment actually matters.<br /> <br /> That being said, the Urges of Green Sun Princess should maybe not often be something so narrow as killing a specific person, and they're stated to be something that's supposed to generally complement the motives and nature of the character.</div> </div> </div> </div>hmm, in that case maybe base the time intervals on the exact urge and situation? So if Lytek is standing before me i have to ignore my urge in order not to kill him right away. But if he also has an army of celestial lions with him then it doesn't count, similar to unacceptable orders.<br /> And if i'm only planning his murder(with the actual execution taking a long time) then maybe i can spend some time pursuing leisure. After all the Yozis do the same despite their urges, the ebon dragon steals children's toys, Malfeas dances, SWLIHN plays gateway, only question here is whether this fact gives THEM limit.<br /> <br /> By the way does anyone else dislike the arcane link element of Torment? I am thinking of removing this element, and in return, also removing the capability of infernals to lose limit by indulging in ANY act of villainy. I feel it's better if they are only capable of doing it by committing their urge's patron Act of Villainy.<br /> <br /> Any thoughts?<br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1492-mark","name":"mark","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1492_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1379"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-07-27T12:06:53-07:00","id":1327774,"title":"","content":"From an IC perspective, the Urge is supposed to be something which serves the purpose of the Yozi which suits the Green Sun Prince in question.<br /> <br /> OOC the player is picking their Urge.<br /> <br /> Inaction shouldn't grant Limit IMO (unless Lytek is standing right in front of you and you're deliberately passing up the perfect chance to kill him)... but inaction shouldn't be a problem in play.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/899114-the-official-exalted-forum-introduction-thread?p=899399#post899399\" target=\"_blank\">Hi, I'm JohnDoe244</a>. My posts represent my opinions, not facts.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/531-johndoe244","name":"JohnDoe244","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar531_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2958"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-07-27T14:38:50-07:00","id":1327801,"title":"","content":"The situation with MoEP: Abyssal Resonance isn't something you should seek to replicate with Infernals.<br /> <br /> #1 Most people who used Resonance as-written hated it, there's a reason it got alternative rules.<br /> #2 If you're in the minority on point #1 it's worth remembering that Acts of Villainy to reduce Limit are harder to perform than venting Resonance and paying some short-term cost like health levels. Do you really want Infernal PCs constantly marrying people?<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b><a href=\"https://swordofcreation.net/\" target=\"_blank\">Sword of Creation</a> a hub for Exalted related content</b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7-lioness","name":"Lioness","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7_2.png","title":"Moderator","rank":6,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5443"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-07-28T14:29:47-07:00","id":1327965,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lioness</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/infernal-exalted/1327706-how-often-should-second-edition-infernals-gain-limit-from-violating-their-urge?p=1327801#post1327801\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The situation with MoEP: Abyssal Resonance isn't something you should seek to replicate with Infernals.<br /> <br /> #1 Most people who used Resonance as-written hated it, there's a reason it got alternative rules.<br /> #2 If you're in the minority on point #1 it's worth remembering that Acts of Villainy to reduce Limit are harder to perform than venting Resonance and paying some short-term cost like health levels. Do you really want Infernal PCs constantly marrying people?</div> </div> </div> </div>By the way, where do i find those updated rules? Never bothered much with abyssals","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1492-mark","name":"mark","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1492_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1379"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-07-28T14:40:39-07:00","id":1327967,"title":"","content":"The alternate rules are in the appendix of <i>Shards of the Exalted Dream</i>.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>He/him","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/177-thecountalucard","name":"TheCountAlucard","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar177_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10857"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-07-28T15:44:21-07:00","id":1327976,"title":"","content":"The way I see it part of the point of the coadjutor was to function as a sort of mediator on when the build up happens for not fulfilling your Urge. That said so long as one would be deemed to be working in good faith towards their Urge nothing happens. Example, If you got the Urge of obliterating Paragon and you exalted in White Wall you aren't gaining limit because Paragon still exists while you're in transit from White Wall to Paragon. If you were in Gem and proceeded to go to White Wall despite the Urge then unless you have some big plan for destroying Paragon that involves going to the other side of the world you'll probably get limit from time to time.<br /> <br /> Probably once or a chapter or story that the character knowingly defies their Urge and takes no actions towards fulfilling it, with additions happening for incidents where they're given a clear opportunity to uphold/advance the Urge and they don't take it. So if your task was to steal information from the library of Nara-o and you don't know who Nara-o is you're probably safe so long as you're still making good efforts at finding out who he is and things that would advance the goal.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3400-nalak42","name":"nalak42","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3400_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2931"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-07-29T04:28:50-07:00","id":1328059,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>mark</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/infernal-exalted/1327706-how-often-should-second-edition-infernals-gain-limit-from-violating-their-urge?p=1327762#post1327762\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">removing the capability of infernals to lose limit by indulging in ANY act of villainy. I feel it's better if they are only capable of doing it by committing their urge's patron Act of Villainy.<br /> <br /> Any thoughts?</div> </div> </div> </div>If they're Infernal PCs, this is a bad plan. It's a feature that the entire coven can indulge in the same Act of Villainy (even if they don't need to) because there's already enough factors pulling them in wildly different directions, not to mention the repetition required is a recipe for Acts of Villainy to wear out their welcome.<br /> <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b><a href=\"https://swordofcreation.net/\" target=\"_blank\">Sword of Creation</a> a hub for Exalted related content</b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7-lioness","name":"Lioness","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7_2.png","title":"Moderator","rank":6,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5443"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-07-29T11:16:44-07:00","id":1328133,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>nalak42</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/infernal-exalted/1327706-how-often-should-second-edition-infernals-gain-limit-from-violating-their-urge?p=1327976#post1327976\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The way I see it part of the point of the coadjutor was to function as a sort of mediator on when the build up happens for not fulfilling your Urge. That said so long as one would be deemed to be working in good faith towards their Urge nothing happens. Example, If you got the Urge of obliterating Paragon and you exalted in White Wall you aren't gaining limit because Paragon still exists while you're in transit from White Wall to Paragon. If you were in Gem and proceeded to go to White Wall despite the Urge then unless you have some big plan for destroying Paragon that involves going to the other side of the world you'll probably get limit from time to time.<br /> <br /> Probably once or a chapter or story that the character knowingly defies their Urge and takes no actions towards fulfilling it, with additions happening for incidents where they're given a clear opportunity to uphold/advance the Urge and they don't take it. So if your task was to steal information from the library of Nara-o and you don't know who Nara-o is you're probably safe so long as you're still making good efforts at finding out who he is and things that would advance the goal.</div> </div> </div> </div>What's the point in giving such a character that Urge?<br /> <br /> Are we exploring hypotheticals as though this is an actual world that independently exists, or are we looking at this in terms of rules for a game?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-07-29T18:35:41-07:00","id":1328197,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Isator Levi</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/infernal-exalted/1327706-how-often-should-second-edition-infernals-gain-limit-from-violating-their-urge?p=1328133#post1328133\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> What's the point in giving such a character that Urge?<br /> <br /> Are we exploring hypotheticals as though this is an actual world that independently exists, or are we looking at this in terms of rules for a game?</div> </div> </div> </div>Which Urge?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3400-nalak42","name":"nalak42","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3400_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2931"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-07-29T19:39:23-07:00","id":1328209,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>nalak42</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/infernal-exalted/1327706-how-often-should-second-edition-infernals-gain-limit-from-violating-their-urge?p=1328197#post1328197\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Which Urge?</div> </div> </div> </div>Either of them, really. They both strike me as primarily an exercise in exploring the Urge as though it's a thing that independently exists and legalistically determining the full implications of an all-encompassing approach to it, rather than placing it in its proper context of gameplay and narrative.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-07-30T13:25:40-07:00","id":1328367,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Isator Levi</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/infernal-exalted/1327706-how-often-should-second-edition-infernals-gain-limit-from-violating-their-urge?p=1328209#post1328209\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Either of them, really. They both strike me as primarily an exercise in exploring the Urge as though it's a thing that independently exists and legalistically determining the full implications of an all-encompassing approach to it, rather than placing it in its proper context of gameplay and narrative.</div> </div> </div> </div>Eh seems reasonable to me for a Slayer to get tasked with destroying something or killing someone, so end Paragon is fair game there. Secrets from Nara-o's library presumably you'd have a specified individual or group's secrets you're supposed to be swiping.<br /> <br /> I'm not seeing how they wouldn't be reasonable in game as you propose.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3400-nalak42","name":"nalak42","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3400_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2931"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-07-30T15:15:02-07:00","id":1328392,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>nalak42</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/infernal-exalted/1327706-how-often-should-second-edition-infernals-gain-limit-from-violating-their-urge?p=1328367#post1328367\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Eh seems reasonable to me for a Slayer to get tasked with destroying something or killing someone</div> </div> </div> </div>Do you <i>really</i> think that the past that I'm being critical of is the killing or destruction? Seriously? I know I'm not always the most direct speaker, but I cannot fathom how it would be unclear that I'm taking about the specific choices of targets that are alternately at risk of being derailing or causing unnecessary arguments about where the parameters are.<br /> <br /> Why is a character that is unreasonably far away from Paragon being tasked with destroying it? Like, under circumstances that are coming up in an actual game, where a debate is necessary about what does and doesn't provoke a roll for Limit? Is the game not better served by them being directed at something more close by?<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>nalak42</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">Secrets from Nara-o's library presumably you'd have a specified individual or group's secrets you're supposed to be swiping.<br /> <br /> I'm not seeing how they wouldn't be reasonable in game as you propose.</div> </div> </div> </div>The unreasonable part is where it's contrived into the form of &quot;I don't even know who Nara-o is&quot;.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-07-30T18:00:25-07:00","id":1328414,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Isator Levi</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/infernal-exalted/1327706-how-often-should-second-edition-infernals-gain-limit-from-violating-their-urge?p=1328392#post1328392\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Do you <i>really</i> think that the past that I'm being critical of is the killing or destruction? Seriously?</div> </div> </div> </div>Yes actually. You didn't ask or phrase your initial question well at all, so of course I'd have to go with the only reasonable outcome of your questions for the two. Which does lead to the model of &quot;What would the Yozi possibly gain by destroying Paragon&quot; for your first question.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Isator Levi</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/infernal-exalted/1327706-how-often-should-second-edition-infernals-gain-limit-from-violating-their-urge?p=1328392#post1328392\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I know I'm not always the most direct speaker, but I cannot fathom how it would be unclear that I'm taking about the specific choices of targets that are alternately at risk of being derailing or causing unnecessary arguments about where the parameters are.</div> </div> </div> </div>By not being at all clear about it and when request was made for clarification deciding not to clarify and instead ramble about it being a terrible example by virtue of not writing up a campaign to explain how the situation naturally came to be in narrative as opposed to just an example to make the point clear.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Isator Levi</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/infernal-exalted/1327706-how-often-should-second-edition-infernals-gain-limit-from-violating-their-urge?p=1328392#post1328392\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Why is a character that is unreasonably far away from Paragon being tasked with destroying it? Like, under circumstances that are coming up in an actual game, where a debate is necessary about what does and doesn't provoke a roll for Limit? Is the game not better served by them being directed at something more close by?</div> </div> </div> </div>Well groups are a thing that happen. Mayhaps your newly exalted Infernal is being tasked alongside several other Infernals to get the job done, maybe your character has a personal history that connects with Paragon and the new exalt practically considered it another signing bonus. Hell for a character conflicted on the goal maybe they'd heard stories about the place from traveling merchants and had always wanted to see it and there's a bit of conflict about over the part where the bosses kindly made your job include going there because they seem to have misunderstood why you wanted to go since they told you to burn it. Out of character maybe the player wanted to be a foreigner and the game was being set in the South and that was the explanation for why they were there to meet up with the rest of the PCs.<br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Isator Levi</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/infernal-exalted/1327706-how-often-should-second-edition-infernals-gain-limit-from-violating-their-urge?p=1328392#post1328392\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The unreasonable part is where it's contrived into the form of &quot;I don't even know who Nara-o is&quot;.</div> </div> </div> </div>Because Infernals are forbidden from asking anyone questions ever? That they are given some sort of instinctive knowledge on all things related to their Urge and thus would have no reason to ask? That Nara-o is a particularly famous diety and therefore its contrived that a character might not know who it is? This isn't a situation that I'm expecting to last infinite time and its hardly contrived for a character not to know who he is.Unless you're viewing gaining an Urge as happening in a direct conversation with your patron Yozi where they lay it all out for you and allow to ask for details its hardly impossible for you not to know all the details on your Urge. You probably ask as soon as a situation crops up where you might think someone knows. Maybe it was almost immediate because your coadjutor was one of those mantis monks that are constantly trying to dig up forbidden lore and therefore Nara-o is well known to it; maybe, it didn't know because while theft is all over the Gethin's wheelhouse secrets aren't usually a big thing for the hunters of rarites.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3400-nalak42","name":"nalak42","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3400_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2931"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-07-30T18:43:50-07:00","id":1328420,"title":"","content":"Oh my gosh, if the character is from whitewall and the urge is destroy paragon, and if the game is going to be set in Paragon, then just have that be part of their background and have them just arrive to paragon. Who cares about the journey there, just have the game start with the character arriving there.<br /> <br /> It's not that hard. No need to make a huge deal about the urge.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3012-uknown-darklord","name":"Uknown DarkLord","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3012_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"485"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-07-30T18:57:42-07:00","id":1328425,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Uknown DarkLord</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/infernal-exalted/1327706-how-often-should-second-edition-infernals-gain-limit-from-violating-their-urge?p=1328420#post1328420\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Who cares about the journey there\u2026</div> </div> </div> </div>I do.<br /> <br /> Generally speaking, the Green Sun Princes we\u2019ve seen have had Urges at least tangentially related to who they are as characters. In what way is Paragon part of the life of this White Waller, enough that he is tasked with laying waste to it?<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Uknown DarkLord</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/infernal-exalted/1327706-how-often-should-second-edition-infernals-gain-limit-from-violating-their-urge?p=1328420#post1328420\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">No need to make a huge deal about the urge.</div> </div> </div> </div>I\u2019m glad I\u2019ve sworn off 2e, since being reminded that some people interpret the Urge as being something the Yozis arbitrarily slap on a character irrespective of the character\u2019s background or skillset is seriously making me not want to play Green Sun Princes.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>He/him","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/177-thecountalucard","name":"TheCountAlucard","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar177_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10857"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-07-30T19:47:21-07:00","id":1328436,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>TheCountAlucard</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/infernal-exalted/1327706-how-often-should-second-edition-infernals-gain-limit-from-violating-their-urge?p=1328425#post1328425\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I do.<br /> <br /> Generally speaking, the Green Sun Princes we\u2019ve seen have had Urges at least tangentially related to who they are as characters. In what way is Paragon part of the life of this White Waller, enough that he is tasked with laying waste to it?</div> </div> </div> </div>Nalak42 brought up the example of the Whitewaller infernal being given the urge to destroy Paragon. So let's go by what he said about it.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Nalak42</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/infernal-exalted/1327706-how-often-should-second-edition-infernals-gain-limit-from-violating-their-urge?p=1328414#post1328414\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Mayhaps your newly exalted Infernal is being tasked alongside several other Infernals to get the job done, maybe your character has a personal history that connects with Paragon and the new exalt practically considered it another signing bonus. Hell for a character conflicted on the goal maybe they'd heard stories about the place from traveling merchants and had always wanted to see it and there's a bit of conflict about over the part where the bosses kindly made your job include going there because they seem to have misunderstood why you wanted to go since they told you to burn it. Out of character maybe the player wanted to be a foreigner and the game was being set in the South and that was the explanation for why they were there to meet up with the rest of the PCs.</div> </div> </div> </div>Hence why I don't care about the journey there. In this hypothetical scenario of a whitewaller infernal being tasked with destroying paragon, it all sounds like it is background for the infernal. Stuff that happens before gameplay actually starts.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> I\u2019m glad I\u2019ve sworn off 2e, since being reminded that some people interpret the Urge as being something the Yozis arbitrarily slap on a character irrespective of the character\u2019s background or skillset is seriously making me not want to play Green Sun Princes. </div> </div> </div>Players set the urge, if they misunderstand that, then hopefully the ST helps them think of an urge that fits.<br /> <br /> As far me saying that it's nothing to make a big deal about, the underlying question is, does the urge strike if not actively working on the urge. If being a whitewaller in paragon is all backstory and prelude to the game starting, then gaining limit from the urge is not something that will happen.<br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":3012,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3012-uknown-darklord","user":"Uknown DarkLord","date":".  Fixed a link 07-30-2019, 10:48 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3012-uknown-darklord","name":"Uknown DarkLord","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3012_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"485"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-07-30T20:51:10-07:00","id":1328445,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Uknown DarkLord</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/infernal-exalted/1327706-how-often-should-second-edition-infernals-gain-limit-from-violating-their-urge?p=1328420#post1328420\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Oh my gosh, if the character is from whitewall and the urge is destroy paragon, and if the game is going to be set in Paragon, then just have that be part of their background and have them just arrive to paragon. Who cares about the journey there, just have the game start with the character arriving there.<br /> <br /> It's not that hard. No need to make a huge deal about the urge.</div> </div> </div> </div>That's a situation that makes perfect sense in terms of gameplay and backstory, but also one in which resolving the conditions in which it accumulates Limit largely irrelevant.<br /> <br /> Same goes with the question of how you'll build Limit if tasked with killing Nara-o before knowing anything about what it is.<br /> <br /> The main thing I'm driving at is that Urge and Torment and the manner in which Limit builds should be almost entirely concerned with player/character choices and dramatic conflict rather than coming up with Urges that are circumstantially difficult to fulfil and figuring out precisely when you need to roll for Limit.<br /> <br /> Angling towards Torment because you're refusing to destroy Paragon for personal reasons or have had an active attempt to do so thwarted strikes me as a lot more dramatic and resonant in a manner that drives a game than it happening as a result of theory craft trying to figure out an Urge that has been tailored towards being impossible to pursue right now.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-07-30T21:29:57-07:00","id":1328448,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Isator Levi</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/infernal-exalted/1327706-how-often-should-second-edition-infernals-gain-limit-from-violating-their-urge?p=1328445#post1328445\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> That's a situation that makes perfect sense in terms of gameplay and backstory, but also one in which resolving the conditions in which it accumulates Limit largely irrelevant.<br /> <br /> Same goes with the question of how you'll build Limit if tasked with killing Nara-o before knowing anything about what it is.<br /> <br /> The main thing I'm driving at is that Urge and Torment and the manner in which Limit builds should be almost entirely concerned with player/character choices and dramatic conflict rather than coming up with Urges that are circumstantially difficult to fulfil and figuring out precisely when you need to roll for Limit.<br /> <br /> Angling towards Torment because you're refusing to destroy Paragon for personal reasons or have had an active attempt to do so thwarted strikes me as a lot more dramatic and resonant in a manner that drives a game than it happening as a result of theory craft trying to figure out an Urge that has been tailored towards being impossible to pursue right now.</div> </div> </div> </div>Okay, but here's the thing that's not how you presented any of your argument. Your argument was &quot;these examples are not anecedotes and therefore are contrived and useless.&quot; When neither of them are even close to impossible to get out of any problems with them. For frack sake dude my example with stealing stuff from Nara-o's library even mentioned you're fine so long as you're making an honest effort to find out who he is. Which is fair game in the part of the book that talks about Urges (pg 28) <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> So long as the Infernals zealously pursue their Urges and unquestioningly accept their punishment when they fail, the Yozi will hold off on punishing them for <i>every</i> perceived misbehavior that falls outside the purview of their Urges. </div> </div> </div>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3400-nalak42","name":"nalak42","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3400_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2931"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-07-31T03:38:05-07:00","id":1328482,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Isator Levi</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/infernal-exalted/1327706-how-often-should-second-edition-infernals-gain-limit-from-violating-their-urge?p=1328445#post1328445\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> That's a situation that makes perfect sense in terms of gameplay and backstory, but also one in which resolving the conditions in which it accumulates Limit largely irrelevant.</div> </div> </div> </div>I'm not sure what you're after. If the game is starting out with a Whitewaller infernal arriving in Paragon, and the urge is to destroy Paragon, who is that circumstantially difficult to fulfill? You're there, and if you choose any actions that strengthen Paragon (unless part of a grand strategy where that is need to bring it to its knees maybe), then you gain limit for going against your urge.<br /> <br /> I guess the player could say, &quot;My character delayed a little in coming, so I am going to start the game off with 2 limit accrued&quot;.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Same goes with the question of how you'll build Limit if tasked with killing Nara-o before knowing anything about what it is. </div> </div> </div>If that were a particular urge, then I'd say if the character doesn't do anything to research anything about Nara-o or do anything in the course of an in game month or two, then they gain limit. <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> The main thing I'm driving at is that Urge and Torment and the manner in which Limit builds should be almost entirely concerned with player/character choices and dramatic conflict rather than coming up with Urges that are circumstantially difficult to fulfil and figuring out precisely when you need to roll for Limit. </div> </div> </div>And with that I agree. It is more difficult to determine when to gain limit if the urge is to kill Nara-O and nothing is known about him. Or if your game is starting in whitewall and you have an urge to destroy paragon. Then yeah, that is going to be harder and more irrelevant as an urge.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3012-uknown-darklord","name":"Uknown DarkLord","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3012_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"485"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-07-31T07:26:41-07:00","id":1328518,"title":"","content":"I think we're all close enough to the same page, and my line of argument is provoking impulses I do not like about myself, so I'm going to leave that part there.<br /> <br /> Hmm, it said that Willpower needs to be spent to disregard Urge, is that supposed to mean that it can't be in the event that a character is empty at the time?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-08-01T04:56:12-07:00","id":1328711,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lioness</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/infernal-exalted/1327706-how-often-should-second-edition-infernals-gain-limit-from-violating-their-urge?p=1328059#post1328059\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">If they're Infernal PCs, this is a bad plan. It's a feature that the entire coven can indulge in the same Act of Villainy (even if they don't need to) because there's already enough factors pulling them in wildly different directions, not to mention the repetition required is a recipe for Acts of Villainy to wear out their welcome.<br /></div> </div> </div> </div>good point. I wonder if the uses are sane enough to also have this apply to the urges they give. Imagine a circle where one person has the urge to kill the perfect of paragon, the other guy is urged to corrupt him, etc. It sure would have been nice to give each coadjutor a phone<img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1492-mark","name":"mark","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1492_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1379"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-08-04T14:39:23-07:00","id":1329337,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>mark</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/infernal-exalted/1327706-how-often-should-second-edition-infernals-gain-limit-from-violating-their-urge?p=1328711#post1328711\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">good point. I wonder if the uses are sane enough to also have this apply to the urges they give. Imagine a circle where one person has the urge to kill the perfect of paragon, the other guy is urged to corrupt him, etc. It sure would have been nice to give each coadjutor a phone<img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" /></div> </div> </div> </div>The coadjutors are &quot;perfectly attuned&quot; to the desires of their Yozi progenitors (at least with respect to their selection of Urges), though. While the Reclamation conspirators don't think alike, they <i>do</i> communicate with each other and have divided the various directions of Creation between them, which <i>should</i> actually work pretty well to avoid screw-ups like this one.<br /> <br /> Cecelyne manages the South. She's certainly a hypocrite, but she's unlikely to contradict herself about something like &quot;what do I want done with the Perfect of Paragon?&quot; for no reason.<br /> <br /> ...Although there's always the Ebon Dragon. It's entirely possible that he would end up betraying one of the other Yozis, or even <i>himself</i>, with whatever he happens to desire at the moment one of his descendant coadjutors is handing out an Urge. Still, even he probably wouldn't sabotage an aspect of the Reclamation without <i>some</i> goal in mind.<br /> <br /> And even if the Yozis were completely disorganized, there are only fifty GSPs and Creation is a <i>huge</i> place. The odds just don't favor things like this happening much.<br /> <br /> On an OOC level, if I had two players show up to the table with mutually contradictory Urges, I would inquire very carefully about what they had in mind.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11237-jefepato","name":"Jefepato","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11237_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"557"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-08-05T03:45:49-07:00","id":1329403,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>mark</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/infernal-exalted/1327706-how-often-should-second-edition-infernals-gain-limit-from-violating-their-urge?p=1328711#post1328711\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">good point. I wonder if the uses are sane enough to also have this apply to the urges they give. Imagine a circle where one person has the urge to kill the perfect of paragon, the other guy is urged to corrupt him, etc. It sure would have been nice to give each coadjutor a phone<img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" /></div> </div> </div> </div>There's an anecdote about two Akuma with conflicting Urges in the Manual. As ST I straight-up wouldn't allow it. Veto. It's derailing.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/899114-the-official-exalted-forum-introduction-thread?p=899399#post899399\" target=\"_blank\">Hi, I'm JohnDoe244</a>. My posts represent my opinions, not facts.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/531-johndoe244","name":"JohnDoe244","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar531_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2958"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}